WEBVTT

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:08.480
Those are pretty.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.370
Are you going to visit your cousin again?

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.200
You sure have excellent timing.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.290
Was it your usual deduction skills,

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.830
or did your yokai friends tell you I was here?

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.570
I have an appointment for 
my eye and leg, as well.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.540
It was pure coincidence.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.860
Ever since that ordeal the other day,

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.100
the ayakashi won't stop talking about you.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.760
"He must be an unrivaled yokai.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:09.760
My lady!

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.610
I bet he's gonna cook us up and eat us!"

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.610
My lady, help!

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.480
I helped you guys out, 
and that's the thanks I get?

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.110
Well, it's your power that scares them.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.120
So your left arm is really okay?

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.620
What? You're actually worried about me?

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:28.370
I'm the one who involved you in all this.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.710
See? It's fine.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.530
Ever since I ate mermaid 
flesh at the age of eleven,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.470
my body always repairs itself,

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.850
no matter how badly it gets hurt.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.730
It's been said that those 
who consume mermaid flesh

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.530
will become immortal 
and gain eternal youth.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:55.480
<b>Mermaid
Diagram</b>

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.110
But I must say that you 
definitely don't look eleven.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:02.050
Yeah... I think that's because the other yokai

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:06.490
whose flesh I ate along with the mermaid's
is nullifying some of the effects.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.000
What was the other one?

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.000
I have to get going.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.050
I'll be late for visiting hours.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.000
Kuro-san.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.390
I actually had a request.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.360
Tonight, I'm going to see a giant serpent

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:29.270
who is the guardian spirit of the 
mountains in the next prefecture over.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.760
Would you come with me?

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.220
A giant serpent in the mountains?

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:33.770
Yes.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:38.280
About ten days ago, one of 
its servants visited me.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.640
It said the guardian is so 
troubled by something

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.030
that it can't even sleep at night.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:48.240
So this is a job for the Goddess of 
Wisdom to the spectres.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.380
You're going to put yourself in danger again?

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.960
You don't even have any special powers.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.000
How rude!

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.700
I have a very special power

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:02.300
that allows me to talk to the 
ayakashi and even touch ghosts!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.970
But that's it, right?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.420
You don't have superhuman strength, 
or the ability to fly,

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.230
or talismans to create 
supernatural phenomena.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.980
You don't have any physical 
or spell-like powers.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:16.670
What if you run into another 
violent, aggressive monster

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.270
like the other day again?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.190
If you're so worried about me, 
you should just come with me.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:25.330
If you were to help out despite 
how much they fear you,

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.120
I'm sure it'll make negotiations 
and mediations go much smoother.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.330
I can't tonight.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.330
Huh?

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.790
I want to enjoy the pork 
miso soup I made last night.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.290
So go by yourself.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.050
Honestly!

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.010
Why is he like that?!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.680
Who lets a poor defenseless 
girl go off into the mountains

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.500
on her own in the middle of the night?!

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.680
I'm terribly sorry it's so late, my lady.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.020
Oh! The swamp is coming into view.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:20.210
I humbly thank you for 
traveling so far to see me,

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.650
my lady.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:29.390
It's no problem. 
That is my duty, after all.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.470
There's no need to thank me.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.710
You were once worshiped as a water god.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.490
It's only natural that I come 
to see you if you need me.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:45.200
It's been quite some time since the 
humans worshiped me as a water god.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.270
The small shrine has long been forgotten,

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:50.330
and no one offers me anything 
for it to rain anymore.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.420
Though, even when they 
did pray to me for rain,

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.460
I never had the ability to control 
the weather to begin with.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:58.170
So it is presumptuous that 
they ever considered me a god.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.920
It's no wonder I've been forgotten.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.300
The human world develops so quickly that

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.800
there are many things I don't understand.

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.960
That is why I sent one of my 
servants to summon you, my lady,

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:15.560
so I could borrow some of your great wisdom.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.560
So, well...

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:22.600
I do apologize that I cannot be more 
hospitable here in these mountains,

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.000
but please do not be angry with me.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.030
Oh, no! It's totally fine.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.280
If I seem to be in a bad mood,
it isn't because of you.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.280
It's due to something personal.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.580
Something personal?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.790
Indeed.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:41.200
I have a boyfriend named Sakuragawa Kuro.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.980
I asked him to accompany me here tonight,

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:46.760
but he declined, saying he'd rather 
stay home and eat pork miso soup.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.510
<b>Sakuragawa</b>

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:54.220
So you had some yokai track me...

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.710
Kuro-san! Please take a look at this!

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.290
You actually did make pork miso soup?

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.400
Don't just go barging into people's homes!

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.020
Wait...

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.570
You're going into the 
mountains dressed like that?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.900
Well done, Kuro-san! 
I knew you had good taste!

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.910
It's my spring apparel! 
My "I've been invited" dress!

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.540
But you were invited into the mountains...

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.540
Wait, no! You shouldn't be so forceful!

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.540
Come on. Just stay still.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:22.050
Wh-What is this?

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.910
The jacket I wore when I went 
mountain climbing in grade school.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.400
How did you dig this up so quickly?!

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.850
Now what are you doing?!

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.300
It's bug repellent.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.320
What do you think you're... doing...

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.520
Here, take some pork miso soup with you.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.410
And some rice balls, too.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.020
Wait...

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:46.730
Kuro-san!

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.100
Don't do anything rash again.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:52.630
So you see, even though I told him

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.950
I would be meeting a giant serpent 
that might like to eat humans,

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.700
he had no intention of coming.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:02.120
Goodness, no! I would never 
dream of eating you, my lady!

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.430
Besides, humans are too 
hard to eat, with the clothes

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.720
and metal accessories they put on...

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.170
So you have actually eaten some before?

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.220
I can't say that I haven't...

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:16.750
I was rumored to be a man-eating 
serpent back in the day,

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.250
but humans don't particularly 
taste that good.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.530
And nowadays,

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:24.070
it would cause far too much trouble, 
so I prefer to avoid that.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.190
By the way, my lady,

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.720
if you were able to bring your soup here,

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.580
couldn't your boyfriend have 
brought his to eat here, too?

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:39.450
Er, I mean, he probably didn't have 
another thermos! That must be it!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.210
We've gone off track. 
Let's get to the issue at hand.

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:49.500
You're concerned about the murdered 
corpse you found in your swamp, right?

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.000
Yes. I cannot fathom why 
that woman came all the way

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.610
to my swamp to dispose of the body,

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:59.850
so I'd like to hear an explanation 
I can be satisfied with.

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:05.600
About a month ago, 
on April 23rd, just past 2 PM,

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:08.690
two hikers who were picking 
mountain vegetables

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.610
found a man's body here at Tsukuna Swamp.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.490
Because he had been stabbed in 
the chest with a sharp knife,

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.310
they ruled his death a murder.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:21.620
However, despite a few days 
passing since he was murdered,

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.360
and him having no cellphone or ID,

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.620
they were able to identify him immediately.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:30.130
Yoshihara Hiroo

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:30.130
Yoshihara Hiroo, 35 years old. 
He worked for a large construction firm.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.880
Eventually, a 30-year-old woman 
was arrested as a suspect.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.880
Tanio Aoi.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.730
It was me.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.890
They got a confession from her.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.890
While many unanswered questions remain,

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.890
they're working mostly on 
gathering evidence right now.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:50.900
It's pretty much an open and shut case.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.000
I assume she threw the body 
into the swamp to hide it,

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.400
or perhaps to delay its discovery?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.450
Nay! It was not to hide the body!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.910
I just happened to see her 
as she dumped the body...

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.890
That woman did, indeed, do something 
so spiteful as to throw that corpse

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:28.320
into this swamp whose water 
I drink from time to time.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.550
But there are times when 
animal corpses float in it,

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:33.370
as well as humans who throw trash into it.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:37.490
So I have the ayakashi that live in 
these mountains clean it regularly.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.240
That's fine and all,

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:43.240
but there's still something 
amiss about all of this.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.880
The woman didn't put anything on the body

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.000
to weigh it down when she threw it in.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:52.500
So the corpse rose to the top 
and was discovered immediately.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:57.260
Above all, at that moment, 
I heard the woman clearly say...

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.260
I really hope they find you.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.220
Despite taking the time and effort 
to dispose of the corpse here,

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.920
she talked about how she 
wanted him to be found.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:15.170
At first glance, it does seem 
her actions don't make sense.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:17.360
Indeed! I don't understand it at all!

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.350
It must be difficult for a woman 
to push a wheelbarrow

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:23.120
with a body in it up a mountain at night.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.870
The police had some doubts about that 
as well, and asked her about it.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:30.750
"Why did you bother carrying 
this corpse to this swamp?"

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.250
And that's when the suspect, Tanio Aoi, said...

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.890
There's a huge serpent living in that swamp,

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.270
and I've heard that it eats people,

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:42.820
so I thought if I dumped the body 
there, the serpent would eat it.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.530
It was a rather irrational confession,

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.740
so it even appeared in newspapers.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.020
<b>Dead Man Found
in Mt. Tsukuna</b>

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.020
I saw that confession, as well.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:56.420
Tanio Aoi's family home is right 
at the base of this mountain.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.800
It could be she actually believed the legends

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:01.250
she'd heard as a child
about a man-eating serpent.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:05.280
And in a desperate attempt, 
she brought the corpse up here...

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:10.860
Of course, that's not the case. 
She was actually trying to hide the body.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:14.170
She wasn't trying to bury it 
or let it sink into the swamp.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.110
She just wanted you to devour it.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:21.170
Then what about what that woman 
said when she dumped the body?

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.320
She didn't mean it as,

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:28.070
"I brought it all the way here, 
so I hope someone will find it."

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:32.640
What she meant was that she 
hoped you would find the body.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:36.770
Nay! Even if I had found the body, 
there was no guarantee that I'd eat it.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.730
If the woman truly wished 
to dispose of the body,

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:44.280
she would've said, "I truly hope it eats you."

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:48.450
<i>For being so huge, this guardian really 
gets hung up on minute details.</i>

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:52.020
This brings up another question.

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:55.280
Why did that woman give a false confession?

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.230
<i>This is going to take a while...</i>

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:02.210
It was probably to hide the real reason 
she threw the corpse into the swamp.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:06.970
Aye. I would like to hear an 
answer I can be satisfied with.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:16.980
What the Guardian Serpent Heard

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.140
Let's go back over the details of this case.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:25.740
You seem rather wise, but we need to make 
sure there aren't any discrepancies.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.230
It all started five years ago.

00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:32.370
Tanio Aoi had a boyfriend 
named Machii Yoshikazu.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.170
But he died with a different woman,

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:40.380
who was his coworker, in what 
looked like a double suicide.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:45.170
Machii worked in the accounting 
department of a large construction firm,

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.150
but after he died, it came to light that

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:50.140
he had messed with some numbers 
and embezzled a large sum of money.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:53.840
Machii realized he wouldn't be 
able to hide the fact that he had

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.390
embezzled the money, so he convinced 
the woman to die with him.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:59.050
Or, at least, that was what everyone believed.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.400
Aoi was deeply hurt by this and returned here

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.190
to her family home at 
the base of Mt. Tsukuna.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.080
She lived as a shut-in for about two years,

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.660
but she eventually found a job near home

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.710
and began to gradually 
get back on her feet.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.920
And it was right around that time...

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.670
On Friday, April 21st of 
this year, around 7:30 PM,

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:28.260
Yoshihara Hiroo showed 
up at Tanio Aoi's house.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.430
I want to apologize for what 
happened five years ago.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:35.390
Yoshihara was a coworker of Machii's, 
so Aoi knew his name and face.

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:40.400
I'm the one who killed Machii, and I'm 
the one who embezzled the money!

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:44.400
Machii and that woman 
realized that and told me

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.490
that if I didn't confess, 
they'd make this public.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.620
That's why I killed them...

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.620
Yoshihara Hiroo's plan went accordingly.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.350
He got away with the embezzlement,

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.500
and it's said he was living 
a decent life afterwards.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:02.650
But starting this year, he was 
met with a series of misfortunes.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:06.230
He made a huge mistake at work.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:08.190
His wife and child died in an accident.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:12.230
On top of that, they found a 
malignant tumor in his body.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.390
Truly a series of unfortunate 
events he never expected.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:19.140
Yoshihara thought this was happening 
because of the incident five years ago,

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:23.310
so he visited Aoi to repent for his crimes.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:27.350
He thought that if he showed remorse now, 
he could escape all this fateful punishment,

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:30.740
and that he might at least 
get away with his life.

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:33.950
I'm so sorry...

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.930
I'm so sorry!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:43.390
That pretty much sums up 
Tanio Aoi's confession.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:47.960
Apparently, Yoshihara had also 
contacted Machii's younger brother,

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.920
asking if they could meet up soon

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.090
regarding what had happened five years ago.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:57.470
Machii's brother was busy at the time, 
so he couldn't talk to him in detail.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.600
That probably prompted 
Yoshihara to go see Aoi first.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:05.340
As the investigation went on,

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:08.370
the embezzlement and supposed 
double suicide came back to light,

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.860
and they also learned that the person 
connected to the prior case, Tanio Aoi,

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.120
lived at the base of the mountain 
where the corpse was found,

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:15.550
and made the connection.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:23.150
Yoshihara-san was about my size, and his 
body had wasted away due to his illness,

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:25.880
so it wasn't much trouble 
to get him up the mountain.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.430
The next day, Saturday the 22nd,

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.280
no one came to the swamp,

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.480
possibly because it rained that day,

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:35.890
so the body wasn't discovered 
until two days later, on the 23rd.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:39.910
I figured the serpent wouldn't want 
to eat his wallet and cellphone,

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.390
so I removed them.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.810
I burned his employee ID back at my house,

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.750
and I threw the knife into 
the swamp with the body.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.010
But...

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:51.150
It didn't eat him.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:56.660
The police have been coming to this swamp 
quite often during the day recently.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.660
It would seem they are looking for that knife.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.520
I'm sure they'd have a 
hard time finding it here.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:07.410
So, did the suspect throw anything 
in along with the corpse?

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:09.380
Hm, I'm not certain...

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.670
Sadly, the information I can get is limited,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.390
so I'll have to use my imagination 
to fill in some holes...

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.340
But I still believe the suspect 
dumped the body into the swamp

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:22.320
for a very simple reason.

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:24.390
A simple reason?

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:25.320
Yes.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.980
In most cases like this, 
it's to protect the real killer.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:32.460
Yoshihara Hiroo had contacted 
Tanio Aoi beforehand,

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:35.240
saying he'd like to come see her.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.680
He was connected to a 
very dark part of her past.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:39.490
Do you think she'd agree to see him alone?

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.120
That is a good point, but...

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.070
No one would suspect anything
if she had someone

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:45.830
with her when Yoshihara came over.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:49.500
Oh, I know. I think Machii's younger 
brother would be a perfect example.

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:52.500
Yoshihara told Machii's 
brother on the phone that

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.260
he had also contacted Machii's former girlfriend.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:59.010
He might have had a bad feeling 
about that and contacted Aoi.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:03.850
After learning the truth of his brother's 
death, he impulsively killed him.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:09.960
But he still had a future.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:14.480
On the other hand, Aoi had been living 
as a shut-in and had very little to lose.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:18.240
That's why she decided she would protect him.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:20.990
After sending the real killer away,

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.990
she decided to dump the corpse 
at the swamp in the mountains.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.780
There are three reasons for this.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.750
First, to let the swamp water 
wash off any traces of

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:31.750
the true killer that may have
ended up on the corpse.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.170
Second, to give the true killer an alibi.

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:42.330
But then why did the woman say, 
"I really hope they find you"?

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.870
This is why the third reason exists.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.920
Tanio Aoi tried to get rid of any 
trace of the true killer at her house.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.150
If she carefully cleaned every inch of 
her house, that could be possible.

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.150
But what about outside the house?

00:18:57.810 --> 00:19:01.140
There's no telling what traces 
could've been left behind.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:05.370
And that's why Aoi threw 
the corpse into your swamp!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:07.200
What do you mean?

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.310
What else? She wanted it to rain!

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.680
You were known as a water god and

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:16.010
received prayers for rain 
in the past, didn't you?

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:20.240
If it poured, tire tracks and anything 
he might've accidentally dropped

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:22.300
would get washed away.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.760
A moment, please...

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.480
I was regarded as a water 
god a very long time ago.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:31.770
Besides, dropping a body into the 
swamp as an offering is unheard of!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.310
And did they honestly think 
they'd be blessed with rain

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.760
by throwing in the corpse of 
a filthy middle-aged man?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.530
If they wanted to give me an offering,

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.530
it should've been a beautiful, living girl!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:44.740
Give me a girl as a sacrifice!

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.280
Er, Guardian?

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.850
There are usually two types of rain rituals.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:54.010
First is to pray to a water god 
and have them grant your wish.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.540
That'd be the orthodox method.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:20:00.270
But there is also the opposite method 
of making the water god angry

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:02.880
so that they go on a rampage and make it rain.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.930
Oh, I do believe I've heard 
that somewhere before.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.140
And it appears that you were indeed enraged.

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:14.350
Goodness me... And it 
actually did rain the next day.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:18.640
So, this explains why you 
heard her say what she did.

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:24.110
Tanio Aoi wanted you to find 
the corpse and go berserk.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:29.120
That's why she let "I really hope they 
find you" slip out without thinking.

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.500
Nay! That explanation is still lacking!

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:38.450
In that case, wouldn't she have said, 
"I really hope it actually does pour,"

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:43.760
or, "I really hope the 
giant serpent gets mad"?

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.180
Of course!

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:51.640
If somebody visited from outside by car, 
someone would've witnessed it.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.990
The police would be investigating that, too,

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:57.520
to see if there might've been 
another killer or accomplices.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:01.030
Y-You seem to deny your own 
claims rather readily...

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.780
That's why the only suspect is Tanio Aoi.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:08.160
Most of what she confessed 
to the police is true.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.010
I think the only thing that's different is

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:12.710
the reason she dumped the 
corpse into this swamp.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.640
Kuro-san!

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:37.560
So that is my lady's boyfriend... 
How terrifying...

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.250
Who said I was your boyfriend?

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.120
So you came after all.

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:45.770
At least correct him! 
Tell him I'm not your boyfriend!

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:48.390
We can have our lovers' quarrel later.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.200
Right now, we have to resolve 
any lingering questions he has.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:54.200
P-Precisely, my lady.

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:57.430
And how are you planning to do that?

00:21:57.430 --> 00:22:00.810
I wish you would've come out sooner 
if you were listening this whole time.

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:01.950
My lady!

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:08.380
So what is the real reason the suspect 
threw the corpse into this swamp?

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:16.250
To Be Continued

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:46.940
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:46.050 --> 00:23:48.480
A wave of incidents involving a phantom 
killer threatens Makurazaka City.

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:51.400
The culprit is a faceless 
woman wearing a red dress.

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:54.160
Are the incidents really 
caused by Steel Lady Nanase,

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:56.240
the ghost of a former idol?

00:23:56.870 --> 00:23:58.820
Next time, "The Rumors of the Steel Lady."
